From: TacoRocket
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: direct NV12 output matching RGBA + scale_vulkan

Apply on libplacebo v7.360.1 (cee9b076f2c63104ccfd497fa79c39a867293ec4).

Adds pl_renderer_set_nv12_output(). With PL_NV12_OUTPUT_MATCH, the renderer
writes both planes of an NV12 target in the final color pass, with the same
result as format=rgba followed by FFmpeg's
scale_vulkan=format=nv12:out_range=limited, without the RGBA image or the
second pass. PL_RENDERER_NV12_OUTPUT in <libplacebo/renderer.h> marks the API,
so callers can compile it in only against a library that implements it. The
default (PL_NV12_OUTPUT_OFF) leaves the renderer unchanged.

- RGB is left unencoded and dithered to 8 bits exactly as the RGBA output
  is dithered, so each pixel holds the texel value the RGBA route writes.
- Those values are read back through a 256-entry UNORM8 ramp texture with a
  linear sampler, the conversion scale_vulkan's texture() read applies.
- scale_vulkan's BT.709 matrix (ff_fill_rgb2yuv_table, as a dynamic mat4),
  limited-range scale and offset and top-left UV store follow, unchanged.
- Y and UV use imageStore, the store scale_vulkan uses. A fragment producer
  keeps its stage, stores Y itself and discards into an unwritten scratch
  attachment; a compute producer's own store is used.

Limited-range BT.709 8-bit targets only. Even-aligned picture rectangles
inside bars are supported; dithering keeps final-frame coordinates through an
internal origin-aware helper (the public dithering API is unchanged).
Unsupported layouts, hooks or capabilities restore the deferred RGB encode
and keep the normal output path.

On Intel ANV (i3-1220P, Gen12) the NV12 output is byte-identical to the RGBA
route at 1920x1080, 1440x1080 pillarbox, 1920x800 letterbox and 1280x720,
and on 2160p HDR10 and Dolby Vision 8.1 sources downscaled with scale_vaapi.
On nine Intel generations (Skylake through Panther Lake, Mesa 25.2.8) the two
routes compile to the same arithmetic; chroma on other hardware also depends
on scale_vulkan's unordered 2x2 chroma writes, which compilation cannot
settle. Other drivers have not been checked.

LGPL-2.1-or-later.
